# Keep the working tree LF on every platform, which is what .editorconfig already
# declares for this repo (end_of_line = lf) and what the committed blobs already are.
#
# Without this, a Windows checkout gets CRLF — git's core.autocrlf default there — and
# any test whose fixture is a multi-line string literal silently gains \r\n, because an
# F# triple-quoted literal carries whatever line endings its SOURCE FILE has. Six
# SyncDocs section tests fail that way on a stock windows-latest runner while passing on
# a Windows dev box whose clone happens to be LF.
#
# This aligns the checkout with the declared intent; it does not change any committed
# content. Note it also masks, rather than fixes, replaceSections not handling CRLF
# DOCUMENTS — which is a separate, user-facing concern and is filed as its own issue.
* text=auto eol=lf
